---
import "@/styles/global.css"

/**
 * The title from before JavaScript: the island replaces it as soon as it knows
 * the verdict, through `documentTitle` in lib/pages.ts, which follows the same
 * format.
 */
interface Props {
  title?: string
}

const { title = "sitesolide" } = Astro.props
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <!--
      The logo's mark, as a data URI rather than a file: the Caddyfile's shared
      snippet serves .svg files as immutable for a year, and a favicon frozen
      for a year can no longer be corrected. Carried by the HTML, it revalidates
      with it. The block fills the whole square here, without margin, so the
      slits stay visible at sixteen pixels.
    -->
    <link
      rel="icon"
      href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 32 32'%3E%3Cdefs%3E%3ClinearGradient id='f' x1='1' y1='1' x2='31' y2='31' gradientUnits='userSpaceOnUse'%3E%3Cstop offset='0' stop-color='%23b3253f'/%3E%3Cstop offset='1' stop-color='%237d1730'/%3E%3C/linearGradient%3E%3C/defs%3E%3Cpath d='M7.32 1H24.68A6.32 6.32 0 0 1 31 7.32V9.92H11.11A1.42 1.42 0 0 0 11.11 12.76H31V24.68A6.32 6.32 0 0 1 24.68 31H7.32A6.32 6.32 0 0 1 1 24.68V22.08H20.89A1.42 1.42 0 0 0 20.89 19.24H1V7.32A6.32 6.32 0 0 1 7.32 1Z' fill='url(%23f)'/%3E%3C/svg%3E"
    />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <!--
      The theme is set before the first render, rather than in a React effect:
      a switch after the fact would show as a white flash on every opening.

      A choice made through the theme button is remembered under the key
      `theme`, `light` or `dark`, and wins over the system. Without it, the page
      follows the system for as long as it stays open, a dashboard being able to
      sit for hours in a tab while the workstation goes dark at nightfall.
      Clearing the key brings back the system, and a choice made in another tab
      is picked up here through the `storage` event. `localStorage` can throw on
      mere access: the page then follows the system.

      `color-scheme` is set inline so that native controls follow from the first
      render; the rule in styles/global.css is now only the fallback.

      This script cannot import src/lib/theme.ts. It repeats its key, its
      validation and its resolution, and tests/theme.test.ts runs it against
      them.

      The script is inline, which assumes that this project's Caddy block sets
      no Content-Security-Policy; the day it sets one, this script will need a
      hash.
    -->
    <script is:inline>
      ;(() => {
        const root = document.documentElement
        const dark = window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)")
        const choice = () => {
          try {
            const value = window.localStorage.getItem("theme")
            return value === "light" || value === "dark" ? value : null
          } catch {
            return null
          }
        }
        const apply = () => {
          const theme = choice() ?? (dark.matches ? "dark" : "light")
          root.classList.toggle("dark", theme === "dark")
          root.style.colorScheme = theme
        }
        apply()
        dark.addEventListener("change", apply)
        window.addEventListener("storage", (event) => {
          if (event.key === "theme" || event.key === null) apply()
        })
      })()
    </script>
    <!--
      The sidebar's collapsed state is read before the first render too: the
      page served by Caddy shows a skeleton of the shell while the session is
      being checked, and its column must already have the right width, otherwise
      it would jump from 16 to 3 rem when React arrives.

      A second script rather than an addition to the first, which
      tests/theme.test.ts runs on its own. It repeats the key and the value from
      src/lib/sidebar.ts, and tests/sidebar.test.ts runs it against them. A storage
      that throws leaves the sidebar expanded.
    -->
    <script is:inline>
      ;(() => {
        try {
          if (window.localStorage.getItem("sidebar-collapsed") === "1") {
            document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-sidebar-collapsed", "1")
          }
        } catch {}
      })()
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-background text-foreground min-h-svh antialiased">
    <slot />
  </body>
</html>
